    "title": "Acrepro.com presents: Wednesday Night LIVE Purdue football chat REPLAY - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dub Jellison ,\n7 hours ago\nPurdue football chat, the 9:00 p.m. show, with Tom Dienhart and Dub Jellison with lively discussion leading into Purdue’s home matchup against Illinois on Saturday.\nAudio Only\nOne bold statement: A .500 October As October is prepared to dawn, Purdue sits with a 2-2 record with eight games to go. No one expected miracles this season. Progress? Yes. How much progress from a win-loss standpoint coming off a 1-11 abomination? Most felt three or four wins–and be competitive in losses–would suffice. Purdue is on track.\nAnd October features what looks like three winnable games: At Minnesota, at Northwestern vs. Rutgers. Could the Boilermakers go 2-1 or 3-0 vs. those foes?\nTo enter a challenging November (at Michigan, Ohio State, at Washington, Indiana) with a 4-4 or 5-3 record would be impressive. And, it seems possible.\nMore: The 3-2-1: Maturation of a QB, October possibilities, respect for Bret and more",
